0.6.0 -> 0.10.0 migration notes:
- VectorCraft shape creation commands now accept geometry only. Coco creates
  ellipse/rectangle geometry first, then applies fill, stroke and stroke weight
  with paint.setFill, paint.setStroke and stroke.set.
- select.all now excludes hidden and locked artwork. Coco's source capture uses
  this behavior intentionally, so hidden/locked production helpers are not
  accidentally adopted as new source art.
- layer.move can deselect artwork moved into hidden or locked layers. Coco's
  generated Cut, Bleed, White and Varnish layers remain visible and unlocked,
  and affected operations explicitly restore the intended selection.
- Coco calls vectorcraft_trace::trace_mask directly for cut generation. The new
  UI Image Trace scaling behavior therefore does not alter Coco's fixed 288 PPI
  cut pipeline.
- The 0.10.0 upgrade requires Rust 1.95 and adds upstream craft-ui/craft-print
  dependencies. Coco's focused format, strict Clippy and test suites pass at
  this pin.

Local PDF export fixes (2026-10-27; retain when updating upstream):
- Spot ink with a white alternate color must not lose overprint under
  discard_white_overprint; that setting is for process white.
- Non-isolated opacity groups with overprinting contents must preserve the
  backdrop rather than knocking out underlying process separations.
- Regressions live in pdf/src/tests_layers.rs, engine/src/cmd/fileio/tests_pdflayers.rs,
  and Coco's production_ink_exports_* PDF/AI tests (including Ghostscript separations).
